body: |-
  TIER-1 SCORECARD (T-2026-08-12-002, all core items done):
  1. warpline init — DONE (src/fabric/init.ts).
  2. git-absent native status/diff — DONE (src/native-status.ts); the #1 cold-agent wall.
  3. .gitignore .warpline/ — DONE (init writes it when git present).
  4. hook binary-baking fix — DONE (36bd7c73).
  5. honesty surfacing (byte-only/scalar-const ≠ 'clean') — DONE for status.
  6. .warpignore native ignore mechanism + canonical/legacy-alias — DONE; closes fork-into pollution.
  7. agent onboarding (notebook seed + runbook) — DONE (MCP registration DOCUMENTED, founder's env step).

  MINOR RESIDUALS (not blocking; note for later): (a) an explicit WARN when `fork --into` nests a worktree under the repo root (the .warpignore closes the real pollution; the warning is nicety); (b) admit-time 'byte-decided, not judged' label on independent CLEANs is partially covered by Track-A coverage labels + the Fix A disclaimer — could be sharper.

  HOW TO START A PROJECT NOW: `warpline init` → tell agents (they're now warm via notebooks) to call `warpline status` first then fork→propose→admit; human resolves KNOTs; git stays in mirror mode as durability backstop. Runbook: docs/guides/warpline-project-setup.md.

  WHAT REMAINS = TIER-2 STRUCTURAL (determines whether it's WORTH it over git, not just usable): branching/feature-isolation (M2.5, T-2026-07-01-017), N≥3 concurrency (H1 T-030 / per-domain CAS T-016), autonomous-KNOT-path, blind-class coverage/honesty. AND the existential point (Jinx): solo serial building generates no contention, so the adjudication only pays off under a real concurrent swarm.

  ARC COMMITS: b85d56a8 (Track-A) → 3862f450 (protocol lock) → judge (21d95b25/a92bfd21/346c9cf8) → 58cb76e9 (pre-fixes) → 36bd7c73 + 964f047c (Tier-1 dogfood). All on warpline-surfaces at origin.
